        "Maintaining ongoing medical fitness for flight involves both the periodic formal medical examination, resulting in the issue or renewal of a medical certificate, and the pilot's continuous personal responsibility for honest self-assessment before every individual flight, since day-to-day fitness can genuinely vary due to factors, minor illness, poor sleep, recent alcohol, that a periodic medical examination conducted months or years apart cannot capture.",
