        "Other toxic hazards in a cockpit environment can include fumes from de-icing fluids, cleaning products, or, in some circumstances, smoke from an electrical or engine fire, each carrying its own specific risks and appropriate immediate response, generally involving securing fresh air ventilation, addressing the source if safely possible, and landing as soon as practicable if symptoms or hazard indications persist.",

