        "Carburettor icing, distinct from airframe icing, can occur even in apparently clear air at temperatures well above freezing, given the additional cooling effect of fuel vaporisation and the pressure drop within the carburettor venturi, and requires timely application of carburettor heat at the first sign of unexplained power loss or, proactively, when operating in conditions known to favour carburettor icing, rather than waiting until a more serious power loss has already developed.",

